read-waker

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Let a thread blocked in event::read be woken: a public ReadWaker, taken before the read starts, makes the read return ErrorKind::Interrupted, so a-tui can stop its input thread and hand the terminal to an editor without losing a key.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream crossterm exposes a way to wake a blocked synchronous read.
